    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i hear that, but it feels like a lot of that \"long term\" stuff is pretty speculative, u know? like, how can a small shop justify massive upfront costs for something that might happen in 10 years? seems like the actual, immediate reality for these owners is just losing money to meet these mandates. do u think the benefits are actually real or just more of an ideological thing?",
